.TH EDISCOPE 1 "2026-11-27" "EDIScope 2.0" "User Commands"
.\"------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
ediscope \- DAB+/EDI diagnostic player
.\"------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ediscope
.\"------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B EDIScope
receives, plays and inspects a DAB/DAB+ ensemble carried as EDI (AF packets
with ETI, e.g. from ODR-DabMux) over TCP or UDP (unicast or multicast, with
PFT and Reed-Solomon FEC), or stored in an ETI-NI or EDI file. Both DAB
(MP2) and DAB+ (AAC-LC, HE-AAC, HE-AAC v2) services are supported.
.PP
Its window shows the ensemble's services and sub-channels (with the CU
occupancy of the multiplex), the Dynamic Label (with DL Plus) and the MOT
Slideshow of the selected service, audio level, spectrum, stereo and phase
correlation meters, the EDI timing (margin delay) and the date/time, and
gives access to the following tools:
.TP
.B Links
Service linking (FIG 0/6), Frequency Information (FIG 0/21) and OE Services
(FIG 0/24).
.TP
.B RadioDNS
RadioDNS (ETSI TS 103 270) resolution of every service, stage by stage, and
the Service Information it leads to.
.TP
.B SPI / EPG
Service and Programme Information (ETSI TS 102 371/102 818) carried in the
ensemble: services, programme schedules, groups and logos.
.TP
.B FIG Analysis
Repetition of every FIG, checked against the repetition rates of
ETSI TS 103 176.
.PP
The selected service can be recorded (untouched audio stream), and so can
the whole ensemble, as EDI or as ETI-NI.
.PP
A source is chosen in the window: an EDI URI
.RI ( tcp:// host : port ,
.RI udp:// host : port
or
.RI udp:// multicast-group : port )
or a file
.RI ( file:// path ,
or "Open EDI/ETI File..."). A file is played at the fixed pace of one frame
per 24 ms, regardless of the timestamps it may carry.
.\"------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B M
Mute/unmute.
.TP
.B R
Start recording the selected service, or stop the recording in progress.
.TP
.BR 1 " ... " 0
Select the 1st to 10th service (as listed); with
.BR Alt :
the 11th to 20th.
.TP
.BR \- " / " +
Select the previous/next service.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy the Dynamic Label to the clipboard.
.\"------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ediscope/ediscope.conf
Settings: recordings folder, toolbar shortcuts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ediscope/network_history
The last 20 EDI sources connected to successfully.
